  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial performance of water and wastewater SPs and RWUs improved.</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">100 SPs were trained during the first program year (30% of all SPs) so the accumulative total is 60%.
In the second program year an additional 20% of the SPs will be trained, so the total will be 80% by the end of the second year. This is a cumulative process. Hence, the target was realized.
12 tariffs were reviewed by the WSRC and submitted to COM during the first program year which is clearly less than the agreed planning. 
Financial working ratio is part of the performance monitoring, and it was monitored for all SPs.
On the tariff compliance by SPs, the COM has not endorsed any submitted tariff yet. Therefore, no compliance was measured.
The original plan was to develop and submit the draft incentive program during the first program year. This was however, not realized.</narrative>
   </description>
